#. TRANSLATORS: display_name
#: actors/bosses/otaman/otaman.tscn
msgid "The Otaman"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/boss_news.tres
msgid "The renegade Otaman is dead? By your hand?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/boss_news.tres
msgid "Then the Sich owes you more than words. Take this, and drink to the ones he killed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/captives_all.tres
msgid "All three are home. The drummer among them asked me to give you this. He says it beats truer for a free man."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/captives_first.tres
msgid "One of our captives walked in this morning, thin as a reed, and said a Cossack broke his cage."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/captives_first.tres
msgid "There are two more. Here, for your trouble."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/idle.tres
msgid "Three of ours sit in cages: one in the cave, one in the crypt, one in the barracks. Break the bars."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/idle.tres
msgid "Three letters lie where their riders fell: in the hideout, the barracks and the works."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/idle.tres
msgid "And if your purse is heavy, the church in the crypt keeps an alms box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "You walk like a man with nowhere to be. Good. I have work."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "Captives in cages, letters in the mud, a church with an empty box. Ask me again and I'll tell you where."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/letters.tres
msgid "Is that the Sich's seal I see in your belt?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: text
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/letters.tres
msgid "Hand over the letters"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: text
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/letters.tres
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/return.tres
msgid "Not yet"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/letters_done.tres
msgid "Every letter is home. The Kosh will know where the boats are, and the powder, and the riders."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/elder/dialogues/letters_done.tres
msgid "This edge was a scout's. It turned many blows; let it turn yours."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: display_name
#: actors/npcs/elder/elder.tscn
msgid "Elder"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/arrival.tres
msgid "Another one walking the graves at dusk. The steppe doesn't see many visitors who mean to leave again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/arrival.tres
msgid "See the stone on the hill? An old otaman lies under it, with his sabre and his oath."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/mound.tres
msgid "Quiet up there now. Quiet is good."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/mound.tres
msgid "Rest when you need to. The fire by the door burns for anyone the steppe hasn't claimed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: speaker
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/raider_shout.tres
msgid "Raider"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/raider_shout.tres
msgid "The keeper's guest! Open the gate, lads, we'll have his boots as well!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/road.tres
msgid "The kurgan stood here before the Sich did. It will stand after."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/road.tres
msgid "Go up to the stone once the raiders are dealt with. Kneel, and listen."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/vigil_end.tres
msgid "You went up, and you came back down. He let you go, then."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/vigil_end.tres
msgid "I'll keep watch at the foot of the hill from now on. He sleeps easier with someone near."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/warning.tres
msgid "There. He has heard you."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/keeper/dialogues/warning.tres
msgid "Raiders camp past the palisade, digging for his silver. Mind them, and go up to the stone when they're gone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: display_name
#. speaker
#: actors/npcs/keeper/keeper.tscn
#: levels/rooms/test_kurgan/logic.tscn
msgid "Grave keeper"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/done.tres
msgid "Sit a while, son. A song is shorter than the road, but it goes with you."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/hint.tres
msgid "You smell of the crypt, but your hands are empty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/hint.tres
msgid "Strings roll far. Try the far west end, past the restless pages."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "Who walks there? A heavy step. A Cossack's step."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "I am blind, son, but not deaf. And my kobza is deaf now: a string broke, and the spare rolled away in the old crypt, west of the house."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "These fingers can't find it in the dark. Yours could."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: text
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "I'll look for it"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: text
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/intro.tres
msgid "Find it yourself"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/reminder.tres
msgid "No string yet? The crypt is west of the house. Mind the dripping stones."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/return.tres
msgid "That smell... wax and gut. You found my string!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: text
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/return.tres
msgid "Give him the string"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/thanks.tres
msgid "There. Hear it? Now the songs have their voice back."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lines
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/dialogues/thanks.tres
msgid "Take this. It is what the songs earned me this month, and you earned it more."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: display_name
#: actors/npcs/kobzar/kobzar.tscn
msgid "Old kobzar"
msgstr ""

#: actors/player/abilities/upgrades.gd:90
msgid "Max health"
msgstr ""

#: actors/player/abilities/upgrades.gd:91
msgid "Max spirit"
msgstr ""

#: actors/player/abilities/upgrades.gd:92
msgid "Flasks"
msgstr ""

#: actors/player/abilities/upgrades.gd:93
msgid "Flask healing"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/blades/guarding_edge.tres
msgid "Guarding edge"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/blades/guarding_edge.tres
msgid "A wide guard made for parrying. Parry window +0.1 s and riposte window +0.25 s, but maximum health -10."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/blades/guarding_edge.tres
msgid "Forged for a hetman's guard, who were never meant to strike first. They waited, turned the blow aside and answered once. The edge is notched only near the hilt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/blades/heavy_edge.tres
msgid "Heavy edge"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/blades/heavy_edge.tres
msgid "A thicker, heavier edge. Damage +30%, but the dash recovers 0.3 s slower."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/blades/heavy_edge.tres
msgid "A smith in the borderlands made it from a ploughshare when the village had nothing left to plough. It cuts like a man who has lost his field."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/blades/thirsting_edge.tres
msgid "Thirsting edge"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/blades/thirsting_edge.tres
msgid "A blade that drinks. Hits have a 30% chance to heal 3, but damage -10%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/blades/thirsting_edge.tres
msgid "Taken from a raider who would not die. The steel stays warm after a fight, and the scabbard is always dry, no matter the rain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/bitter_root.tres
msgid "Bitter root"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/bitter_root.tres
msgid "Chewed against marsh fever. Poison damage taken -50%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/bitter_root.tres
msgid "The marsh villages chew it at dawn and spit at dusk. It tastes of earth and regret, and the fever passes them by."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/brass_bell.tres
msgid "Brass bell"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/brass_bell.tres
msgid "Its ring stirs the spirit. Each hit gives 1 more spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/brass_bell.tres
msgid "Once it hung from a church eave and called the faithful home. Now it calls something else, with every blow struck."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/clay_amulet.tres
msgid "Clay amulet"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/clay_amulet.tres
msgid "Fired clay that has seen worse flames. Fire damage taken -50%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/clay_amulet.tres
msgid "Shaped by a potter whose kiln burned down twice. The third time, he wore it into the fire to fetch his tools and walked out again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/hare_foot.tres
msgid "Hare foot"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/hare_foot.tres
msgid "A charm for those who would rather not be caught. Run speed +15%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/hare_foot.tres
msgid "Steppe children carry one to outrun bad luck. Grown men carry one and do not say why."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/healer_knot.tres
msgid "Healer's knot"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/healer_knot.tres
msgid "A knot of red thread tied by a village healer. Each flask heals 15 more."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/healer_knot.tres
msgid "Each turn of the red thread is a prayer the healer would not say aloud. She tied it for her son, who never came back for it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/hunter_tally.tres
msgid "Hunter's tally"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/hunter_tally.tres
msgid "A stick with a notch for every kill. Each kill heals 5."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/hunter_tally.tres
msgid "Every notch was cut with the same knife, by the same hand. The last notches are shallow, as if the hand had grown tired."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/iron_cross.tres
msgid "Iron cross"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/iron_cross.tres
msgid "A plain iron cross on a leather cord. Maximum health +15."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/iron_cross.tres
msgid "Plain iron, hammered by a novice monk who left the monastery for the Sich. He kept the cross and gave away the rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/quick_bracer.tres
msgid "Quick bracer"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/quick_bracer.tres
msgid "A tight leather bracer that frees the wrist. Swings wind up and recover 20% faster."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/quick_bracer.tres
msgid "Laced so tight it leaves marks. The fencing masters of the Sich wear them until the wrist forgets it was ever slow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/raven_eye.tres
msgid "Raven eye"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/raven_eye.tres
msgid "A black bead that finds the weak spot. Critical hit chance +15%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/raven_eye.tres
msgid "Ravens follow armies across the steppe and always find the soft places first. This bead is said to have been one of their eyes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/red_sash.tres
msgid "Red sash"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/red_sash.tres
msgid "Worn by those who fight on when they should fall. Damage +25% while health is below 30%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/red_sash.tres
msgid "The sash is red so the blood does not show. Its owners were known for standing up one more time than they should have."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/war_drum.tres
msgid "War drum"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/war_drum.tres
msgid "A small drum that beats after every kill. Damage +20% for 5 seconds after a kill."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/war_drum.tres
msgid "Small enough for a boy to carry into battle. He beat it for every fallen enemy, and the company fought harder to hear it again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/charms/wolf_fang.tres
msgid "Wolf fang"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/charms/wolf_fang.tres
msgid "A fang from a steppe wolf, bound in wire. Damage +10%."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/charms/wolf_fang.tres
msgid "The wolf took three sheep and a dog before a shepherd's boy took its fang. The wire was his mother's, from a broken loom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/black_sea_storm.tres
msgid "Duma of the Black Sea Storm"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/black_sea_storm.tres
msgid "Sing it for 15 spirit: pillars of fire rise on both sides at once."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/black_sea_storm.tres
msgid "A storm split the Cossack fleet in two, and each half was sure the other had drowned. The duma ends with both halves landing on the same shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/burning_steppe.tres
msgid "Duma of the Burning Steppe"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/burning_steppe.tres
msgid "Sing it for 15 spirit: eight pillars of fire march forward along the ground."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/burning_steppe.tres
msgid "The kobzar sang of the summer the Tatars set the grass alight, and of the riders who turned the fire back on them. Old men say the steppe still remembers the tune."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/calm_sea.tres
msgid "Duma of the Calm Sea"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/calm_sea.tres
msgid "Sing it for 15 spirit: everything close around the singer is stunned for a moment."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/calm_sea.tres
msgid "After the storm the sea went so still that the gulls forgot to cry. Enemies near the singer forget, for a breath, what they were doing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/iron_hand.tres
msgid "Duma of the Iron Hand"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/iron_hand.tres
msgid "Sing it for 20 spirit: for 20 seconds every swing hits heavy and deals 25% more damage."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/iron_hand.tres
msgid "Sung before a charge, fist on the saddle. The hand that strikes after it is said to weigh as much as the horse beneath it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/road_home.tres
msgid "Duma of the Road Home"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/road_home.tres
msgid "Sing it for 30 spirit: the road folds, and the singer stands again at the last fire they rested by. Wounds stay as they are. It falls silent while a great foe bars the way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/road_home.tres
msgid "Mothers taught it to sons riding out to the Wild Field, so they could find the way back. Most sons forgot it. The ones who remembered came home old."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/sabre_ring.tres
msgid "Duma of the Sabre Ring"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/sabre_ring.tres
msgid "Sing it for 20 spirit: three sabres circle the singer for 15 seconds, cutting enemies and stopping shots."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/sabre_ring.tres
msgid "A song for the last of a company, back to back in the reeds. It names every sabre that fell, and while it is sung they are said to stay close."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/three_brothers.tres
msgid "Duma of the Three Brothers"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/three_brothers.tres
msgid "Sing it for 10 spirit: three shots fly forward, one after another."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/three_brothers.tres
msgid "Three brothers fled Azov on foot, and only the youngest came home. The duma gives each of them one shot, and the listeners never agree on which one missed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: title
#: actors/player/items/dumas/thunderbolt.tres
msgid "Duma of the Thunderbolt"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: description
#: actors/player/items/dumas/thunderbolt.tres
msgid "Sing it for 20 spirit: a bolt of thunder falls on the singer, striking hard everything around them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: lore
#: actors/player/items/dumas/thunderbolt.tres
msgid "Sung only under an open sky. A blind kobzar sang it once in a church and was never asked back, though the roof was mended by spring."
msgstr ""

